# Supabase CLI scratch state — never commit.
#
# `supabase link`, `db push` and `functions deploy` write cached project state
# under supabase/.temp/. Two reasons this must be ignored:
#
#   1. CREDENTIALS. supabase/.temp/pooler-url contains the pooled Postgres
#      connection string, password included. Without this rule a routine
#      `git add -A` commits a live database credential.
#
#   2. It broke the deploy pipeline. deploy-production.ps1 fails a dirty
#      working tree, on purpose — if the artefact being deployed is not the
#      artefact in version control, a rollback has nothing to return to. But
#      the Supabase CLI creates .temp/ as a side effect of `supabase link` in
#      step 5, so the very act of running the pipeline made the tree dirty and
#      failed the next run. Generated scratch is not uncommitted work.
#
# Matches the layout `supabase init` generates.

.temp
.branches

# Local dev stack artefacts (not used here, ignored for safety).
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
